    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "so if i do this regularly, does it actually change my baseline stress levels or is it just a temporary fix? i'm interested in the long term physiological effects, like if it helps with neuroplasticity or something.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Regular practice of box breathing can absolutely lead to long-term physiological changes, moving it beyond just a temporary fix. Consistent activation of the parasympathetic system through controlled breathing helps to \"retrain\" your nervous system, making your baseline state less reactive to stressors. Over time, this consistent calming effect can lead to measurable reductions in chronic cortisol levels and potentially influence neuroplasticity by promoting a more resilient state in your brain. It's like building a stronger, less easily agitated internal defense system.",
      "source": "target",
